    {
      "key": "treehouse.lesson.house-making.imps-layers.explanation",
      "source": "**Imps** is the image editor. A project keeps layers, masks and text as editable structure — not a flattened blob. Saving a managed edit captures a preimage first, so the original is recoverable from the project's history. Gallery assets are Files assets; Imps is where you edit them.",
      "placeholders": [],
      "kind": "structured-prose",
      "status": "live",
      "locations": [
        "src/openclank/treehouse_field_guide.py:944"
